/// A unit named as a qualifier in a case other than its declaration.
///
/// Qualified access goes through Environment's Imports rather than through the
/// scope chain, so it is a third lookup path and can be fixed independently of
/// the other two.
///
/// The 'uses' clause itself is a separate question, and this file deliberately
/// spells it exactly.  A 'uses' names a file, and whether the file is found at
/// all is the file system's decision, not the language's -- so on a
/// case-insensitive volume 'uses ''lib/caseunit''' locates the file and then
/// fails the unit-name check, while on a case-sensitive volume it fails to open
/// anything.  Folding the qualifier is well defined; folding the 'uses' is not,
/// and this suite takes no position on it.
///
/// Fails with: Undefined variable 'CASEUNIT'.
///
uses 'lib/CaseUnit';

test 'A unit qualifier resolves through any spelling of its name';
begin
    AssertEqual ('hello', CASEUNIT.Greet ());
end
